From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:53:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe: The MAT for runtime images loaded late

After ReadyToBoot the memory attributes table is installed again at
every allocation of runtime memory. A runtime driver loaded then gets
its pages, its fixup data and its EFI_RUNTIME_IMAGE_ENTRY that way, and
only after them InsertImageRecord() adds the record of its sections:
the table describes the image as runtime code without an image, RO and
XP, until some later allocation of runtime memory installs it again.
An OS that applies the table, as macOS does, can then neither run the
code of the driver nor write its data. OpenCore loads OpenRuntime after
ReadyToBoot, and its SyncRuntimePermissions quirk corrects the table
for it. edk2 master has the same code.

InsertImageRecord() installs the table again once the record is in,
after ReadyToBoot only: before it nothing changes, and a record that
cannot be made leaves the table as it was.

TEST=OpenShell from an ESP, on the W541 payload in a q35 ROM: after
"load" of a runtime driver with .text and .data that allocates nothing
as it starts, MmapDump of OpenCore 1.0.8 lists its pages in the table
as runtime code RO|XP, merged with the unused pages of the runtime code
bin; with the patch, its header and .data are XP and its .text RO.
OpenRuntime of OpenCore 1.0.8 comes out split without the patch too,
by an allocation of runtime memory that follows its record. The smoke
test of the payload passes, the runtime services moved as boot.efi of
macOS moves them included.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv

---
 MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Misc/MemoryAttributesTable.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Misc/MemoryAttributesTable.c b/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Misc/MemoryAttributesTable.c
index 7f4d703..4a9e469 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Misc/MemoryAttributesTable.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Misc/MemoryAttributesTable.c
@@ -656,6 +656,15 @@ InsertImageRecord (
 
   SortImageRecord (&mImagePropertiesPrivateData.ImageRecordList);
 
+  //
+  // After ReadyToBoot the table was installed again when the pages of this
+  // image were allocated, before its record existed: without this, the image
+  // keeps the attributes of runtime code without an image (RO | XP).
+  //
+  if (mMemoryAttributesTableReadyToBoot) {
+    InstallMemoryAttributesTable ();
+  }
+
 Finish:
   if (EFI_ERROR (Status) && (ImageRecord != NULL)) {
     DeleteImagePropertiesRecord (ImageRecord);
-- 
